# The web image's test environment (P1.27): the images workflow starts the built image with it and waits for its
# HEALTHCHECK. Test values only; no secret. The media origin must be another site than the public one (plan §5.2).
# Since P2.04c the server also needs Postgres, the seal keyring and the OAuth client keys: the workflow makes those
# secrets per run and sets the keys that describe its throwaway database (P2.04i); the app's own settings stay here.
# Since P2.05 sign-in needs our PDS's host and the handle suffix it gives (the test values of test-env.ts).
UNSET_ENV=test
UNSET_SERVICE=http
UNSET_COMMIT=1111111111111111111111111111111111111111
LISTEN_PORT=8080
PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://unset.test
HTTP_ALLOWED_HOSTS=unset.test
TRUSTED_PROXY_MODE=socket
MEDIA_ORIGIN=https://media.other.test
PG_POOL_MAX=4
PLC_URL=https://plc.directory
PDS_HOSTNAME=pds.unset.test
HANDLE_SUFFIX=.pds.unset.test
# Legal placeholders (P2.15). Unquoted: Docker --env-file keeps quotes as part of the value.
PRIVACY_OFFICER_TITLE=[to fill: PRIVACY_OFFICER_TITLE]
PRIVACY_OFFICER_CONTACT=[to fill: PRIVACY_OFFICER_CONTACT]
SUPPORT_EMAIL=[to fill: SUPPORT_EMAIL]
SECURITY_CONTACT=privacy-page
SECURITY_TXT_EXPIRES=2027-10-01T00:00:00Z
